meta {
  name: 01. Create Settlement
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/groups/{{settlementGroupId}}/settlements
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "to_member_id": {{settlementToMemberId}},
    "amount_toman": {{settlementAmountToman}},
    "note": "Bank transfer",
    "attachment_ids": {{settlementAttachmentIds}}
  }
}

docs {
  # 01. Create Settlement

  **Method:** `POST`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/groups/:groupID/settlements`
  **Auth:** Required

  ## Description


  Register your own external payment to another active member of this group. Any active recipient is accepted; the future simplified debt graph can provide the frontend default, but the API does not require that receiver. Partial payments, overpayments and payments when no debt exists are permitted.

  If amount exceeds your current positive net debt among active group members, registration still succeeds with `warnings[0].code=PAYMENT_EXCEEDS_CURRENT_DEBT` and message `payment exceeds your current net debt in this group; registration is allowed`. This is an advisory based on current expenses and SUCCESS payments; pending/rejected/canceled payments do not reduce debt. It is not a receiver-specific debt check or a balance report API.

  All persistence and receipt linking are atomic. Repeating a successful POST creates another payment; no idempotency key is implemented. Disable duplicate form submission in the frontend. A successful Create is 201.



  All routes require Bearer authentication, an ACTIVE account and ACTIVE membership with left_at=null. Membership IDs belong to this group; user IDs are not interchangeable with them. An owner or site ADMIN has no special payment permissions.

  Group status enum: `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING`, `CLOSED`. Both ACTIVE and SETTLING allow settlement writes; CLOSED allows reads only. Expenses, polls and draws remain frozen whenever the group is not ACTIVE.

  Payment status enum (uppercase, case-sensitive): `PENDING`, `SUCCESS`, `REJECT`, `CANCELED`. PENDING and CANCELED are visible only to their active sender/recipient. SUCCESS and REJECT, including receipts, are visible to every active group member. Filtered list counts follow the same visibility rules.

  Payments cannot be edited. Only the active sender may soft-delete PENDING. Only the active recipient may confirm/reject PENDING. Confirmation records a successful external payment; this endpoint does not perform a bank transfer. Rejection/cancellation never count as successful payments. Owner/admin cannot override either party.

  A sender who leaves loses access; their existing PENDING payment remains answerable by its active recipient. If the recipient leaves/is removed before responding, incoming PENDING payments become `CANCELED` and record `canceled_at` in the same transaction. Rejoining does not revive them. Former-member financial relationships are outside the active-member balance calculation; history remains stored. `is_external` is true when either party currently has inactive membership/left_at. Membership status values remain ACTIVE/INACTIVE.

  IDs are manual environment variables. No response script sets or overwrites settlement IDs. Set settlementGroupId, settlementToMemberId (from Get Group Members), settlementId, and settlementAttachmentIds yourself. Auth login/refresh keeps its existing token behavior.


  ## Request


  | Field | Type | Required | Rules |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | to_member_id | integer | Yes | Another ACTIVE membership in this group, with ACTIVE account. |
  | amount_toman | integer | Yes | 1..9223372036854775807 TOMAN; no fractional amount. |
  | note | string or null | No | At most 2000 Unicode characters; no NUL. |
  | paid_at | RFC3339 string or null | No | External payment date. Omitted/null defaults to server time. |
  | attachment_ids | integer array or null | No | At most 100 unique positive IDs of your unbound SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT uploads. Omitted/null/[] means no receipt. |

  Do not send from_member_id, user_id, status or group_id in JSON; the authenticated user/path determine them. The existing JSON binder ignores unrelated fields.

  Upload optional receipts first using 07. Upload Settlement Receipt (the shared attachment API). Upload success alone does not register a payment. Copy uploaded IDs to settlementAttachmentIds, e.g. [1201]. Each receipt must be yours, unbound, and have no group or this same group. A receipt already linked to a payment/expense cannot be reused.

  Warning example (in data.warnings; HTTP remains 201):

  ```json
  [{"code":"PAYMENT_EXCEEDS_CURRENT_DEBT","message":"payment exceeds your current net debt in this group; registration is allowed"}]
  ```


  ## Response


  | Response field | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | from_member_id / to_member_id | Group membership IDs. Sender is always derived from the access token. |
  | from_member / to_member | Current display name, member_id, user_id and nullable avatar_url. |
  | amount_toman | Positive signed BIGINT integer in TOMAN. |
  | paid_at | User-supplied RFC3339 external payment date, or server time when omitted/null. |
  | confirmed_at / rejected_at / canceled_at | Server decision time; other outcome timestamps stay null. |
  | created_at / updated_at | Registration time / last state change time. |
  | is_frozen | True only when the group is CLOSED. |
  | is_external | Either party has left/is no longer active; retained history. |
  | can_confirm / can_reject / can_delete | Permissions calculated for the authenticated caller. UI hints; backend always enforces authorization. |
  | attachment_ids | IDs of attached SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT files; [] when none. |
  | attachments | Receipt metadata: id, original_filename, mime_type, file_size_bytes, nullable access_url. |
  | warnings | Create-only advisory messages; [] for other successful operations. |


  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 701,
      "group_id": 10,
      "from_member_id": 30,
      "to_member_id": 31,
      "from_member": {
        "member_id": 30,
        "user_id": 3,
        "name": "Ali",
        "avatar_url": null
      },
      "to_member": {
        "member_id": 31,
        "user_id": 4,
        "name": "Reza",
        "avatar_url": null
      },
      "amount_toman": 100000,
      "status": "PENDING",
      "note": "Bank transfer",
      "paid_at": "2026-11-18T10:00:00Z",
      "confirmed_at": null,
      "rejected_at": null,
      "canceled_at": null,
      "created_at": "2026-11-18T10:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-18T10:00:00Z",
      "is_frozen": false,
      "is_external": false,
      "can_confirm": false,
      "can_reject": false,
      "can_delete": true,
      "attachment_ids": [],
      "attachments": [],
      "warnings": []
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid IDs, amount, query, timestamp or JSON; note over 2000 characters. |
  | 400 | `SETTLEMENT_SELF_PAYMENT` | `you cannot register a payment to yourself` | Sender and recipient are the same membership. |
  | 400 | `SETTLEMENT_DUPLICATE_ATTACHMENTS` | `attachment_ids must not contain duplicate IDs` | Repeated receipt ID on Create. |
  | 400 | `INVALID_FILE_TYPE` | `file type or format is not supported` | A supplied attachment is not SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | No Bearer token. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | Invalid token. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | Expired access token; refresh or log in again. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | Revoked access token. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | Caller account inactive. |
  | 403 | `SETTLEMENT_FORBIDDEN` | `you do not have permission to access this settlement` | Caller not an active group member, or non-party reading a PENDING/CANCELED payment. |
  | 403 | `SETTLEMENT_RECIPIENT_REQUIRED` | `only the recipient can confirm or reject this payment` | Confirm/Reject called by anyone other than the recipient. No owner/admin override. |
  | 403 | `SETTLEMENT_CREATOR_REQUIRED` | `only the creator can delete this pending payment` | Delete called by anyone other than its sender. |
  | 403 | `ATTACHMENT_FORBIDDEN` | `you do not have permission to access or modify this attachment` | Receipt belongs to another uploader, already linked or associated with another group. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | Group absent or deleted. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | Caller no longer exists. |
  | 404 | `SETTLEMENT_NOT_FOUND` | `settlement not found` | Payment absent, soft-deleted, or in another group. |
  | 404 | `SETTLEMENT_RECIPIENT_NOT_FOUND` | `recipient must be an active member with an active account in this group` | Recipient membership/account missing, inactive or outside the group. |
  | 404 | `ATTACHMENT_NOT_FOUND` | `attachment not found` | Supplied receipt ID missing/deleted. |
  | 409 | `SETTLEMENT_NOT_PENDING` | `only pending payments can be confirmed, rejected or deleted` | Already SUCCESS/REJECT/CANCELED. Repeating DELETE after soft deletion returns 404. |
  | 409 | `SETTLEMENT_GROUP_CLOSED` | `payments cannot be changed after the group is closed` | Group CLOSED; create/confirm/reject/delete forbidden. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | Unexpected database/internal failure. |
  | 503 | `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` | `storage service is temporarily unavailable` | Receipt/avatar URL resolution unavailable. |

  The table includes shared errors across this folder; individual operations return only applicable cases. Error envelope:

  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "code": "SETTLEMENT_NOT_PENDING",
    "error": "only pending payments can be confirmed, rejected or deleted"
  }
  ```
}
